-- Q21 [Hydrophobicity & Unique Residues] medium skill4 ans=C
WITH q AS (
  INSERT INTO questions (section, topic, subtopic, question_text, options, correct_answer, explanation, difficulty, foundation, content_category, discipline, cognitive_skill, estimated_time_seconds)
  VALUES ('bio_biochem', 'Amino Acids, Peptides, and Proteins', 'Hydrophobicity & Unique Residues', 'A researcher characterizing a globular protein consults a Kyte-Doolittle hydropathy table, on which positive values denote hydrophobic side chains:

| Residue | Kyte-Doolittle value |
| --- | --- |
| Isoleucine | +4.5 |
| Valine | +4.2 |
| Glycine | -0.4 |
| Aspartate | -3.5 |
| Arginine | -4.5 |

Based on these data, the residue most likely to be buried in the protein''s hydrophobic core is:', '[{"label": "A", "text": "Glycine"}, {"label": "B", "text": "Arginine"}, {"label": "C", "text": "Isoleucine"}, {"label": "D", "text": "Aspartate"}]'::jsonb, 'C', 'This is a Biochemistry question that falls under the content category ''Structure and Function of Proteins and Their Constituent Amino Acids.'' The answer is C because on the Kyte-Doolittle scale a positive value denotes a hydrophobic side chain, and isoleucine carries the most positive value in the excerpt (+4.5). The textbook states that side chains with high average hydrophobicity are ''probably buried in the interior of a protein away from the aqueous environment,'' and that ''hydrophobic residues tend to be buried within the protein''s core, while polar and charged residues are generally exposed.'' Reading the most positive value off the table and linking it to burial therefore points to isoleucine. (Choice A) Glycine has a Kyte-Doolittle value near zero (-0.4), the closest to neutral in the table, so it is not the most hydrophobic and gives no strong burial signal. (Choice B) Arginine has the most negative value (-4.5), making it the most hydrophilic; the textbook indicates such polar/charged residues are ''generally exposed to the aqueous environment,'' the opposite of buried. (Choice C) is correct: isoleucine''s value of +4.5 is the most positive (most hydrophobic) in the excerpt, and high hydrophobicity predicts burial in the protein''s nonpolar core. (Choice D) Aspartate has a negative value (-3.5), marking it as hydrophilic and surface-favoring rather than core-buried. This is a Data-based and Statistical Reasoning question because you must interpret the tabulated Kyte-Doolittle values, identify the most positive one, and connect high hydrophobicity to burial in the hydrophobic core.', 'medium', '1A', 'Structure and Function of Proteins and Their Constituent Amino Acids', 'biochemistry', 4, 105)
  RETURNING id
)
